 "transcript": {
  "answer": "Yes. Meals out and takeaway prices in Melbourne are higher than a year ago, and they are rising faster than they were in early 2025.\n\n**Latest figure (August 2026):** Melbourne meals out and takeaway prices were up **3.5%** on August 2025.\n\n**Trend (annual change, Melbourne):**\n- April 2025: 2.6%\n- August 2025: 3.4%\n- January 2026: 3.8%\n- May 2026: 4.4% (the recent peak)\n- July 2026: 4.1%\n- August 2026: 3.5%\n\n**Comparisons for August 2026:**\n- Australia-wide meals out and takeaway rose **4.1%**, so Melbourne is a little below the national figure.\n- Overall inflation (all groups) was **3.5%** in Melbourne and **4.0%** nationally. Melbourne meals out is therefore rising at about the same pace as Melbourne prices generally.\n\nMelbourne's meals-out inflation has been above 3% every month since June 2025, apart from a dip to 2.5% in July 2025. It eased from 4.1% in July 2026 to 3.5% in August 2026, but it is still a firm increase.",
